817 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 106 0 R/E(Creative direction:)/Pg 36 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

818 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 106 0 R/E(My strategy was to never describe the brick, because nobody really buys a brick. They buy what a brick becomes. I start out with a universal truth \(big things start with small things\) and build up to a human hand-off, reframing the brick as the starting point of something enormous, reiterating that the brick itself isn\220t the product, but the potential is.)/Pg 36 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

819 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 106 0 R/E(Assignment)/Pg 36 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

820 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 106 0 R/T(Write a 6-word story that sells something)/E(Write a 6-word story that sells something)/Pg 36 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj

821 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 106 0 R/E(The brief: Noise-cancelling headphones. \(Something I\220m personally a big fan of.\))/Pg 36 0 R/K[8]>>
endobj

822 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 106 0 R/E(The first thing that came to mind was Hemingway\220s \215For sale: baby shoes, never worn.\216 It\220s simple, yet it evokes loss, curiosity, and empathy, in just a few words.)/Pg 36 0 R/K[9]>>
endobj

823 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 106 0 R/E(The world screams. She chose silence.)/Pg 36 0 R/K[10]>>
endobj

824 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 106 0 R/E(Creative direction:)/Pg 36 0 R/K[11]>>
endobj

825 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 106 0 R/E(It doesn\220t mention the product, and doesn\220t need to, because it sells the feeling of putting on noise-cancelling headphones without talking about them at all.)/Pg 36 0 R/K[12]>>
endobj

826 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 106 0 R/E(Additionally, the first 3 words establish the problem \(\215the world screams\216\), and the last 3 words establish the solution while framing it as something that\220s within the subject\220s control \(she\220s choosing the silence\). That turns a pair of headphones into an act of agency.)/Pg 36 0 R/K[13]>>
endobj

827 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 106 0 R/E(Self-initiated)/Pg 36 0 R/K[14]>>
endobj

828 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 106 0 R/T(Selling a red brick)/E(Selling a red brick)/Pg 36 0 R/K[15]>>
endobj

829 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 106 0 R/E(The brief: I wanted to see how much possibility I could sell in something as ordinary as a red brick in less than 50 words.)/Pg 36 0 R/K[16]>>
endobj

830 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 106 0 R/E(Everything vast starts with something tiny. An ocean begins as a single drop. This brick is five pounds of that mammoth potential. Entire worlds can start with this brick. Its ancestors have been holding up civilizations, empires, and kingdoms. Lay the first one. History is in your hands.)/Pg 36 0 R/K[17]>>
endobj

